From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:19:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 112/113] x86_64: loads that a loop does not change go before
 it (provenance)

do_hoist_invariant_loads (with SLP, after the vectoriser): in a loop without
calls, a scalar or vector load through a pointer the loop does not change,
from memory that no store of the loop can be (same base and other offsets,
or other fields of elements of the same array, see the provenance in
optslp), goes into a temp before the loop, and so do the packs and
broadcasts of such values. Before a while loop the copy is guarded by the
loop condition; for and repeat loops run their body when they are reached
(a converted for loop has its entry test outside).
nbody: bi^.x/y, bi^.z, bi^.mass and its broadcast leave the inner loop;
tests/test/opt/tslp2.pp.
